WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.638
Screenshots pile up as Screenshot,

00:00:02.638 --> 00:00:06.363
date, time, and nobody can
find the one they need.

00:00:06.363 --> 00:00:08.384
Bowerbird is the file mate.

00:00:08.384 --> 00:00:13.923
It reads them, proposes honest names,
and moves nothing until you approve.

00:00:13.923 --> 00:00:15.258
Bowerbird runs on one PC.

00:00:15.258 --> 00:00:21.040
A PowerShell launcher starts the engine,
and your browser talks to it on localhost.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:26.930
The engine indexes and searches, proposes
renames, and organizes by rules.

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:29.218
The index is encrypted on disk.

00:00:29.585 --> 00:00:31.695
Model calls go through Fairlead,

00:00:31.695 --> 00:00:34.925
with Bowerbird's own key from
Credential Manager.

00:00:34.925 --> 00:00:37.548
The OpenAI key stays in Lazarette.

00:00:37.548 --> 00:00:40.000
Semaphore export and SnapShackle
names exist in the code,
